      "title": "The npm Worm That Fooled Every Trust Signal We Had",
      "description": " A supply chain worm that passes every trust signal (provenance, SLSA, signed commits) just poisoned 420 npm packages in half an hour. It steals AWS keys, npm tokens, and Kubernetes secrets, then publishes infected versions of your other packages. If your CI/CD uses long-lived credentials, assume compromise. Here's how to detect, remediate, and prevent this with CloudTrail, GuardDuty, CodeArtifact, and DNS Firewall.",
